Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g17: return released kept-graph backing without retiring identity

Base: rolotrealanis98/linux 8ab10100a4c1c944797e3fc8345589aff57777df
Upstream: https://github.com/aurora-silicon/linux/pull/1946
Upstream-commit: 3ad9af366a7251892f3ad9ecca21b086de834ddf
Upstream-merge: 2dbf9d53ae5f7dcd8067360988e5688272a01e60

Port the kept-graph housekeeping pass from merged PR1946. Return only the
USC backing to the existing preallocated deferred batch after observing the
final free-list release; retain graph memory, scheduler/control objects and
pool ownership until the firmware can no longer walk the graph. Destruction
of backing mappings remains outside the device mutex. This hardening is not
an explanation or a fix for the observed J716s scheduling-pause recovery.

The pinned M5 implementation differs from the Neo test of PR1946: render
IDs are rebindable, and merely retaining an Arc<RenderPool> does not pin the
physical identity. Transfer the existing pair pin into RetiredBinding at
both parking and owner replacement. This does not allocate, take another
pin, or change a release cursor; the graph's original identity remains held
for exactly the graph's retained lifetime, including the leak-on-no-room
path. A same-context pool replacement also keeps the old identity until its
existing final-release collector permits dropping the retired binding.

Pools::released(id, control) ignores control and accepts missing/out-of-range
leases in this base. Do not use it as a backing-release proof on M5. Match
all fields of the current Owner (pool serial, backing epoch, slot, control,
run-list and cookie) and require a consumed final release with no inherited
release witness. A missing lease is not a validated release. The pool pin
prevents identity/storage reassignment while kept graphs are scanned; vacate
changes only backing residency, never the retained identity or graph.

Keep existing off-lock preparation, logical-owner, runtime-epoch, recovery,
DMA retirement and deferred-capacity gates unchanged. PR1948 explicitly
excludes M5 and is not part of this port; PR1925 logging is not a dependency.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/queue/render.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/queue/render.rs
@@ -2762,2 +2762,5 @@
 pub(crate) struct RetiredBinding {
+    /// M5 identities are rebindable: retain the original pin while firmware
+    /// may still walk this graph, not just an Arc to its logical pool.
+    _pool_pin: Option<crate::g17::freelist::PoolPin>,
     memory: Option<KBox<memory::Memory>>,
@@ -3088,1 +3091,1 @@
-        self.pool_pin = binding.pool_pin.take();
+        let old_pool_pin = core::mem::replace(&mut self.pool_pin, binding.pool_pin.take());
@@ -3094,2 +3097,3 @@
         let retired = RetiredBinding {
+            _pool_pin: old_pool_pin,
             memory: old_memory,
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/queue/render/parked.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/queue/render/parked.rs
@@ -111,2 +111,3 @@
         let retired = RetiredBinding {
+            _pool_pin: self.pool_pin,
             memory: Some(self.memory),
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/render/pools.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/render/pools.rs
@@ -77,0 +78,12 @@
+    /// Proof for returning a retained graph's backing, not just an idle slot.
+    /// M5 identities can be rebound: only this exact backing's owner and its
+    /// consumed final release permit unmapping. Missing leases prove nothing.
+    pub(super) fn backing_released(&self, pool: &RenderPool) -> bool {
+        Self::slot(pool.id())
+            .ok()
+            .and_then(|slot| self.leases[slot])
+            .is_some_and(|lease| {
+                lease.owner() == Self::owner(pool) && lease.released()
+            })
+    }
+
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/render.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/render.rs
@@ -1125,9 +1125,9 @@
 
     /// Gives back the USC backing of render pools whose client VM pressure
     /// reclaim evicted (an idle VM) and whose final free-list release was
-    /// consumed. The vacated backings go to the worker's deferred batch, which
-    /// frees them after the device mutex; a later job of that client re-arms
-    /// the pool first.
+    /// consumed, and of the pools that kept graphs still hold. The vacated
+    /// backings go to the worker's deferred batch, which frees them after the
+    /// device mutex; a later job of an evicted client re-arms its pool first.
     pub(in crate::g17) fn vacate_evicted_render_pools(
         &mut self,
         init: &crate::g17::initdata::InitData,
@@ -1154,2 +1154,16 @@
         }
+        // A kept graph is never staged again. Keep its graph and identity pin;
+        // only its exact backing's consumed final release permits unmapping.
+        for graph in render.kept_graphs.iter() {
+            if !deferred.render_backing_room() {
+                break;
+            }
+            let pool = graph.pool();
+            if pool.vacant() || !render.pools.backing_released(pool) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            if let Some(backing) = pool.vacate() {
+                deferred.defer_render_backing(backing);
+            }
+        }
         Ok(())
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/freelist.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/freelist.rs
@@ -576,9 +576,10 @@
 }
 
 /// A render pool retained by a logical context and every graph referencing it.
-/// Its backing can be given back while the pool's free-list release has been
-/// consumed and the client VM is evicted; a fresh backing is installed before
-/// the pool is staged again.
+/// Its backing can be given back after its final free-list release is consumed
+/// when the client VM is evicted or a kept graph will never stage it again.
+/// The graph retains its pool identity independently of backing residency;
+/// a later staging of an evicted client's pool first installs fresh backing.
 pub(crate) struct RenderPool {
     storage: Arc<RenderStorage>,
     /// Counts installed backings, so a re-armed backing is a new free-list
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime.rs
@@ -1347,1 +1347,1 @@
-    /// Backing of render pools vacated for evicted idle clients.
